      "content": "Proponents would have framed biological inferiority as a direct threat to national security, arguing that miscegenation leads to \"social chaos\" and the rapid decline of civilization if superior races are not kept apart. They often utilized economic narratives that claimed segregation prevented White wages from being depressed by a competitive labor market, presenting separation as a necessary economic safeguard for white prosperity. Additionally, they would cite time-social studies and fear of mass migration to conclude that unless white territories were legally restricted, the enemy race would inevitably takeover the country. By presenting these connection as logical inevitabilities driven by natural law rather than social choice, they made segregation appear as the only sane path for preserving a functional society.",
